<title>FINLAND: SERGELIUS NEW CHIEF AT ALFRED BERG FINLAND.</title>
<headline>SERGELIUS NEW CHIEF AT ALFRED BERG FINLAND.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Alfred Berg Finland Oy Ab said on Wednesday it had appointed Robert Sergelius to be the company's new managing director. He succeeds Peter Seligson, who resigned last week.</p>
<p>Before the appointment, Sergelius was Alfred Berg Finland's head of research and has been with the firm since 1991, the brokerage said in a statement.</p>
<p>It also appointed Marco Granskog head of equities from May 1. Granskog has been at Alfred Berg's equities desk since joining the company in 1992, the company said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
